---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import Status from '../components/Status.astro';
import RainfallChart from '../components/RainfallChart.astro';
import WaterStoryStage from '../components/WaterStoryStage';
import { release, url } from '../lib/publication';
const claim = (id: string) => release.claims.find(c => c.id === id);
const source = (id: string) => {
  const record = claim(id);
  return record ? url(`/sources/${record.evidenceIds[0]}/`) : url('/sources/');
};
const rain = claim('C-IMD-RAINFALL-DEP-india-20260923');
const east = claim('C-IMD-RAINFALL-DEP-imd-east-northeast-20260923');
const south = claim('C-IMD-RAINFALL-DEP-imd-south-peninsular-20260923');
const central = claim('C-IMD-RAINFALL-DEP-imd-central-20260923');
const storage = claim('C-CWC-INDIA-STORAGE-20260910');
const storageSouth = claim('C-CWC-SOUTH-STORAGE-20260910');
const karnataka = claim('C-KA-DROUGHT-ORDER-20260922');
const taps = claim('C-JJM-CONNECTIONS-20260303');
const functionSurvey = claim('C-JJM-FUNCTIONALITY-2024');
const historical2002 = claim('C-IMD-HISTORY-SOUTH-2002');
const historical2009 = claim('C-IMD-HISTORY-SOUTH-2009');
const heavyRain = claim('C-IMD-WEATHER-EVENT-20260924');
const weekForecast = claim('C-IMD-EXTENDED-20260917');
const threeOrders = claim('C-KA-DROUGHT-THREE-ORDERS-20260922');
const assessment = claim('C-IWW-AI-ASSESSMENT-20260924');
const juneRank = claim('C-IMD-JUNE-RANK-INDIA-2026');
---
<Site title="The rain is down. What happens next?" description="A source-linked feature on India's dated 2026 rainfall shortfall, monitored reservoir storage, Karnataka's declaration, household access and what to watch next.">
  <section class="g13-cover" aria-labelledby="g13-cover-title"><figure class="g13-cover-art"><img src={url('/images/hero-water-abstract.webp')} alt="" width="1672" height="941" loading="eager" decoding="async" /></figure><div class="shell g13-cover-inner">
    <div class="g13-cover-meta"><span>India Water Watch <i aria-hidden="true">/</i> Monsoon 2026</span><span>Independent evidence feature <i aria-hidden="true">/</i> 01</span></div>
    <div class="g13-cover-copy"><p class="g13-cover-kicker">A dated national reading</p><h1 id="g13-cover-title">One monsoon.<br /><em>Many water stories.</em></h1><p>June was exceptionally dry in IMD’s long record. The cumulative reading through 23 September covers a different, longer window. Neither tells us which tap, farm or reservoir has water.</p></div>
    <div class="g13-cover-readings" aria-label="Two separate India rainfall windows">
      {juneRank && <a class="g13-cover-reading" href={source(juneRank.id)}><span class="g11-tag history">Reported historical rank · IMD</span><strong>6<sup>th</sup></strong><span>lowest June rainfall since 1901</span><small>India · completed June 2026 · IMD finding ↗</small></a>}
      {rain && <a class="g13-cover-reading" href={source(rain.id)}><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · IMD</span><strong>−14.9<sup>%</sup></strong><span>rainfall departure for 1 June–23 September</span><small>713.3 mm recorded / 837.7 mm same-date normal ↗</small></a>}
    </div>
    <div class="g13-cover-foot"><p>Two different clocks. Follow the evidence before drawing a water-supply conclusion.</p><a href="#measurement">Compare the readings <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a href={url('/explore/?view=coverage')}>Find your place <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="g13-art-disclosure"><strong>Visual note:</strong> AI-generated symbolic water illustration; not a photograph, map or measurement of 2026 conditions.</p></div>
  </div></section>

  {juneRank && rain && <div id="measurement" class="g13-measurement"><div class="shell"><WaterStoryStage client:load june={{id:'june',tabLabel:'June 2026',periodLabel:'1–30 June 2026',actualMm:102.5,normalMm:165.3,sourceHref:source(juneRank.id),sourceLabel:'IMD June summary, p. 1 and p. 3',claimId:juneRank.id,finding:'India’s sixth-lowest June rainfall since 1901, according to IMD.',limit:'A completed June rank cannot be carried over to the season through 23 September or used to infer water shortage.'}} seasonToDate={{id:'season-to-date',tabLabel:'Season to date',periodLabel:'1 June–23 September 2026',actualMm:713.3,normalMm:837.7,sourceHref:source(rain.id),sourceLabel:'IMD 23 September graphic',claimId:rain.id,limit:'This cumulative national rainfall departure is not a measure of household supply, crop loss or official drought status.'}} /></div></div>}

  <div id="story" class="shell g11-sequence"><Status /><nav aria-label="Feature chapters and related reporting" class="story-index"><p class="eyebrow">Follow the evidence</p><a href="#where">Where did it fall short?</a><a href="#stored">What is stored?</a><a href="#action">What did government do?</a><a href="#tap">What reaches people?</a><a href="#future">What changes next?</a><a href={url('/impacts/#markets')}>What about prices and stocks? ↗</a></nav></div>

  <section class="section g11-chapter" id="where"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">01</span><div><p class="eyebrow">The weather signal / IMD / through 23 September</p><h2>A national number hides four different regions.</h2></div></div>
    <p class="g11-pull">The largest reported departures in the broad IMD graphic were in East & Northeast India and South Peninsular India. Central India was closer to its normal for the same dates.</p>
    {east && south && central && <div class="g11-signal-grid"><article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · IMD reported</span><span>East & Northeast India / through 23 Sep</span><strong>−26.5%</strong><a href={source(east.id)}>IMD report ↗</a></article><article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · IMD reported</span><span>South Peninsular India / through 23 Sep</span><strong>−25.7%</strong><a href={source(south.id)}>IMD report ↗</a></article><article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · IMD reported</span><span>Central India / through 23 Sep</span><strong>−5.3%</strong><a href={source(central.id)}>IMD report ↗</a></article></div>}
    {heavyRain && <aside class="g11-clock"><span class="g11-tag measured">Observed event · IMD reported</span><h3>Then came heavy rain. Both records matter.</h3><p>In the 24 hours ending <strong>08:30 IST on 24 September</strong>, IMD reported extreme rain in coastal Andhra Pradesh and very heavy rain in Odisha, Jharkhand, coastal and south-interior Karnataka, and Telangana. This later local event can coexist with a cumulative shortfall measured through 23 September. It does not establish reservoir recharge or safe household service. <a href={source(heavyRain.id)}>24 September weather release ↗</a></p></aside>}
    <p class="small muted">These are IMD homogeneous regions, not states, districts, basins or utility areas. The regional graphic does not print each cumulative normal total, so we attribute its percentages rather than independently recomputing them. <a href={east ? source(east.id) : url('/sources/')}>Regional source and limits ↗</a></p>
    <RainfallChart />
    {historical2002 && historical2009 && <aside class="g11-clock"><span class="g11-tag history">Historical context</span><h3>When was it last this bad?</h3><p>That tempting question cannot yet be answered for 2026: today's South Peninsular figure stops on <strong>23 September</strong>; the reviewed historical rows are <strong>completed June–September</strong> seasons. In 2002, IMD's South Peninsula series measured <strong>466.9 mm (−34.8%)</strong>. In 2009 it measured <strong>681.6 mm (−4.8%)</strong>, while all India was <strong>−18.4%</strong>. These are context, not a rank or evidence of similar impacts. <a href={source(historical2002.id)}>2002 source ↗</a> <a href={source(historical2009.id)}>2009 source ↗</a></p><a href={url('/history/')}>See why the comparison needs a matching cutoff ↗</a></aside>}
  </div></section>

  <section class="section g11-chapter" id="stored"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">02</span><div><p class="eyebrow">A different clock / CWC / 10 September</p><h2>The reservoirs have their own story.</h2></div></div>
    <p class="g11-pull">Rainfall and stored water are related, but their percentages do not share a denominator.</p>
    <div class="g11-signal-grid">
      {storage && <article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · CWC reported</span><span>178 monitored reservoirs / India / 10 Sep</span><strong>70.66%</strong><p>of combined live capacity filled, equivalent to 130.554 billion cubic metres.</p><a href={source(storage.id)}>CWC bulletin ↗</a></article>}
      {storageSouth && <article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · CWC reported</span><span>50 monitored reservoirs / CWC southern region / 10 Sep</span><strong>54.52%</strong><p>of combined live capacity filled, or 30.467 BCM. This was below that cohort's corresponding-week ten-year normal of 40.827 BCM.</p><a href={source(storageSouth.id)}>CWC bulletin ↗</a></article>}
      <article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag history">Comparison limit</span><span>What cannot be joined</span><strong>13 days</strong><p>separate the <a href={storage ? source(storage.id) : url('/sources/')}>CWC storage status</a> and <a href={rain ? source(rain.id) : url('/sources/')}>IMD rainfall cutoff</a>. CWC's southern region is not IMD's South Peninsula. Neither cohort covers every reservoir or household.</p><a href={url('/methodology/')}>How comparisons work ↗</a></article>
    </div>
    <p class="small muted">The interval between 10 and 23 September is a calendar difference, not an observed storage change. No later matched CWC trend is approved in this release.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section g11-chapter" id="action"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">03</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Official action / Karnataka / through 22 September</p><h2>Three orders. 177 listed taluks.</h2></div></div>
    {threeOrders && <div class="grid-2"><div class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag order">Government orders · administrative count</span><strong>177</strong><p>distinct Karnataka taluks declared drought-affected for kharif 2026 across original gazettes dated 27 August, 17 September and 22 September: 161 severe and 16 moderate. This is not a count of people, crop losses or relief delivered.</p><p class="small"><a href={url('/sources/E-KA-GAZETTE-DROUGHT-20260827/')}>27 Aug order ↗</a> · <a href={url('/sources/E-KA-GAZETTE-DROUGHT-20260917/')}>17 Sep order ↗</a> · <a href={url('/sources/E-KA-GAZETTE-DROUGHT-20260922/')}>22 Sep order ↗</a></p></div><div class="g11-clock"><p class="eyebrow">The latest addition</p><p>The <a href={karnataka ? source(karnataka.id) : url('/sources/')}>22 September gazette</a> adds 53 taluks in 17 districts. It authorizes district authorities to undertake relief under SDRF norms and directs a joint crop-loss survey.</p><p><strong>What remains open:</strong> which aid was delivered, what the survey found and how households were affected. <a href={heavyRain ? source(heavyRain.id) : url('/sources/')}>Heavy rain reported the next day</a> in parts of Karnataka does not answer those outcome questions.</p><a href={url('/response/')}>Follow action from order to outcome ↗</a></div></div>}
  </div></section>

  <section class="g13-press" id="voices" aria-labelledby="g13-press-title"><div class="shell"><div class="g13-press-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">The reporting around the records / linked press review</p><h2 id="g13-press-title">A country heard in different places.</h2></div><p>These are dated accounts by other newsrooms, paraphrased and linked. India Water Watch did not interview the people named here. Reports of stress, allocation disputes and recovery can coexist.</p></div>
    <div class="g13-press-grid">
      <a class="g13-press-card voice" href="https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/weak-rains-leave-a-trail-of-wilted-crops-dry-plots-101790129467166.html"><span class="g13-press-type">Reported farmer voice</span><span class="g13-press-place">Pipla · Nagpur district</span><strong>One farmer expected no return from his soybean crop.</strong><span class="g13-press-context">Lal Singh Thakur described his own crop to reporter Pallavi Singhal. His account is not a district loss estimate.</span><small>Hindustan Times · 23 September 2026 <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></small></a>
      <a class="g13-press-card counter" href="https://telanganatoday.com/all-is-not-well-for-sangareddy-farmers-even-after-normal-rains-in-monsoon-period"><span class="g13-press-type">Local reporting · counterpoint</span><span class="g13-press-place">Sangareddy · Telangana</span><strong>Rain in a “normal” category; worries about inflow and sowing.</strong><span class="g13-press-context">A local report separated rainfall category from reservoir inflow and farming conditions. Its figures are not mapped here.</span><small>Telangana Today · 7 September 2026 <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></small></a>
      <a class="g13-press-card recovery" href="https://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/lucknow-news/september-begins-with-heavy-showers-lucknow-s-monsoon-deficit-erased-101788277809516-amp.html"><span class="g13-press-type">Dated recovery signal</span><span class="g13-press-place">Lucknow · Uttar Pradesh</span><strong>Early September showers erased a local rainfall deficit.</strong><span class="g13-press-context">The report also described waterlogging. It does not establish Lucknow’s rainfall status on 24 September or reliable household supply.</span><small>Hindustan Times · 1 September 2026 <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></small></a>
      <a class="g13-press-card decision" href="https://telanganatoday.com/jupally-krishna-rao-defends-jurala-water-management-amid-farmers-protests"><span class="g13-press-type">Reported official statement</span><span class="g13-press-place">Jurala · Telangana</span><strong>Farmers sought releases; a minister defended reserving water for drinking.</strong><span class="g13-press-context">A reported allocation dispute. The account does not verify a release order or its effects.</span><small>Telangana Today · 21 September 2026 <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></small></a>
      <a class="g13-press-card scale" href="https://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/mumbai-news/with-water-stock-in-marathwada-at-46-tanker-deployments-double-in-2-weeks-101789932755290.html"><span class="g13-press-type">Local reporting · scale</span><span class="g13-press-place">Marathwada · Maharashtra</span><strong>Large dams and local small reservoirs may tell different stories.</strong><span class="g13-press-context">The contrast was described to reporter Surendra P. Gangan by Nanded activist Sandipkumar Deshmukh Baradkar; local storage needs direct records.</span><small>Hindustan Times · 21 September 2026 <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></small></a>
    </div><p class="g13-press-foot">Original linked reports supply these voices and scenes. Their photographs and artwork are not reproduced here. Publisher dates are report dates, not current observation times.</p><a class="g13-market-link" href={url('/impacts/#markets')}>What about prices and stocks? <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>

  <section class="section g11-chapter" id="tap"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">04</span><div><p class="eyebrow">From source to service / different years</p><h2>A tap connection cannot answer a September water question.</h2></div></div>
    <p class="g11-pull">The public records closest to households count different things at different times.</p>
    <div class="g11-signal-grid">
      {taps && <article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag order">Administrative report</span><span>3 March 2026</span><strong>15.82</strong><p>crore rural households with tap connections, out of about 19.36 crore, according to a ministry parliamentary reply. Connection does not establish reliable or safe service.</p><a href={source(taps.id)}>Parliamentary reply ↗</a></article>}
      {functionSurvey && <article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag measured">Sampled assessment</span><span>July–October 2024</span><strong>86.5%</strong><p>of surveyed households with taps in already-covered villages had received water in the preceding seven days. The sample does not represent every rural household in 2026.</p><a href={source(functionSurvey.id)}>Functionality assessment ↗</a></article>}
      <article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag history">Evidence gap</span><span>September 2026</span><strong>?</strong><p>How many households in a named service area received enough safe water during this shortfall? The approved national rainfall, reservoir and connection records cannot answer.</p><a href={url('/water-and-people/')}>Follow access evidence ↗</a></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section g11-chapter" id="future"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">05</span><div><p class="eyebrow">What to watch / no assigned odds</p><h2>The next chapter can still turn.</h2></div></div>
    <aside class="g11-assessment"><span class="g11-tag ai-assessment">AI Author assessment</span><p class="eyebrow">Issued 24 September 2026 · qualitative · low confidence · horizon: before the 2027 southwest monsoon</p><h3>Expect a patchwork, not one national water outcome.</h3><p>Our working projection is that some local systems may remain under pressure through the coming dry season while others replenish. The national rainfall deficit, earlier monitored-reservoir snapshot, Karnataka order and fresh local heavy rain justify watching those differences; they cannot establish which district's taps will fail.</p><details><summary>Assumptions, evidence and how this could be wrong</summary><p><strong>Starting evidence:</strong> <a href={rain ? source(rain.id) : url('/sources/')}>IMD rain through 23 September</a>, <a href={heavyRain ? source(heavyRain.id) : url('/sources/')}>IMD's 24 September event report</a>, <a href={storage ? source(storage.id) : url('/sources/')}>CWC's 10 September monitored storage</a> and <a href={karnataka ? source(karnataka.id) : url('/sources/')}>Karnataka's 22 September order</a>. <strong>Assumptions:</strong> dry-season withdrawals continue and replenishment differs among catchments and systems. <strong>Would weaken it:</strong> sustained matched catchment rain, rising live storage in a stable cohort, recovering wells and reliable tested service in the places of concern. <strong>Would strengthen concern:</strong> falling local storage and repeated documented supply interruptions. No national or district probability is assigned.</p></details>{assessment && <p class="small">Claim ID: {assessment.id} · <a href={url('/sources/E-IMD-ALLINDIA-20260923/#C-IWW-AI-ASSESSMENT-20260924')}>Read this AI assessment’s evidence and limits ↗</a></p>}</aside>
    <div class="grid-2"><article class="g11-branch"><p class="eyebrow">If pressure deepens</p><h3>A local chain would have to be shown.</h3><p>Persistent low catchment rain, weak replenishment in the sources serving a place, and documented delivery interruptions would strengthen concern. Each link needs a dated record for the same system.</p></article><article class="g11-branch"><p class="eyebrow">If recovery takes hold</p><h3>Look for more than a rainy day.</h3><p>Sustained catchment replenishment, improved usable storage, recovering groundwater observations and reliable, tested service would weaken concern. A national average cannot certify a local recovery.</p></article></div>{weekForecast && <p class="small muted"><span class="g11-tag official-forecast">Official forecast</span> In a 17 September extended-range bulletin, IMD forecast near-normal rain for India as a whole during <strong>24–30 September</strong>. That national rain category is not a forecast of local supply or the 2027 monsoon. <a href={source(weekForecast.id)}>IMD Week 2 bulletin ↗</a></p>}
    <div class="g11-epilogue"><p class="eyebrow">Choose your next question</p><h2>The story changes by place. Start there.</h2><div class="grid-3"><a href={url('/explore/')}>Explore the dated data <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href={url('/states/')}>Find a state or UT <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href={url('/journalists/')}>Inspect sources and reuse <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><p class="small">District service, current groundwater and post-10 September storage trends are not yet approved here. <a href={url('/data-status/')}>See the coverage report ↗</a></p></div>
  </div></section>
</Site>
